{"kind":"synthesis","scope":{"collections":["iran-fissures"],"subjects":["Iran"],"tags":["synthesis","fissures","overview"]},"synthesis":{"title":"Cracks at depth, 17 Apr – 1 May 2026 — apex, axis, alloy","summary":"Three deeper-cut fissures complete the picture. APEX (the Khamenei family + aghazadeh): a Khamenei niece was arrested on 24 Apr after publicly condemning the regime, while Dominica revoked the Caribbean citizenship of a second Shamkhani-family member on 18 Apr — closing the elite hedging hatch and signalling a visible split inside the apex itself. AXIS (the proxy and external-backer architecture): Lebanese press (Lebanon24, Elsiyasa) on 29 Apr reported that Iran is reducing its support for Hezbollah, while Bloomberg (22 Apr) and RFE/RL (17 Apr) document that Xi Jinping's support has explicit limits — Iran's strategic-depth and external-rescue scenarios are simultaneously cratering. ALLOY (legitimacy in the cultural surface): an organised diaspora movement on 30 Apr–1 May demanded that FIFA ban Iran from the 2026 World Cup ('they are not representing Iran'); a global movement campaigned to halt Toomaj Salehi's execution; the Supreme Court confirmed the Abbasi family death sentences on 27 Apr; healthcare is fragile per MSF on top of 50 reported damaged hospitals; and gold/currency are in 'explosive surge' alongside US-tracked capital flight. The Zayandeh-Rud release is being pushed to late Ordibehesht — re-arming the Isfahan-farmer flashpoint at the worst possible moment. Read together with the prior 19 cracks in iran-cracks/ and iran-margins/, the regime's apex, axis, and alloy are degrading in lockstep — i.e., the failure modes are no longer single-domain.","basis":{"claim_ids":["claim:iran-fissures:20260502:efd29094","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:3dfc2a68","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:1eacd753","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:f2d4765c","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:65688d83","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:60d38fd1","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:99dafc11","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:90859146","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:a491296d","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:a9610792","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:d7a8e3cf","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:bf365adc","claim:iran-fissures:20260502:528c1cd7"]},"limitations":"The Khamenei-niece arrest rests on a single second-tier wire; verify before high-confidence use. Lebanon24/Elsiyasa Hezbollah pieces are directionally clear but qualitatively-framed; magnitude unproven. JaFaJ capital-flight claim is low-tier and should be re-anchored to a Treasury OFAC release before promotion above 'medium' confidence.","status":"active"},"id":"synth:iran-fissures:20260502:4b515f74","schema_version":"knb.v1","created_at":"2026-05-02T00:01:42.721Z","created_by":"agent:claude-research"}
